          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ochanine+elliptic+genus"} Ochanine elliptic genus
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo •
                    %mi SO
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mo •
                  %mo =
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi δ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ϵ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^{SO}_\bullet \to M_\bullet = \mathbb{Z}[\tfrac{1}{2}][\delta, \epsilon]
            lifts to a map of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+spectra"} ring spectra
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %mi SO
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi Ell
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  M SO \longrightarrow Ell
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#LandweberRavenelStong93"}> Landweber-Ravenel-Stong 93
            ). Here
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ell
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 6
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ell[\tfrac{1}{6}]
            is equivalently
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tmf0%282%29"} tmf0(2)
            (
            %a{:href => "#Behrens05"}> Behrens 05
            ) and as such this lift is analogous to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+orientation+of+tmf"} string orientation of tmf
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                    %mi String
                    %mo →
                    %mi tmf
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M String \to tmf
          %p
            If this map of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+spectra"} ring spectra
            could be shown to be “highly structured” in that it preserves
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-%E2%88%9E+ring"} E-∞ ring
            structure, then it would equivalently be a universal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientation+in+generalized+cohomology"} orientation
            (see at
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "orientation+in+generalized+cohomology#RelationToGenera"} relation between orientations and genera
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            After inversion of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prime+number"} prime number
            2, the oriented
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+ring"} cobordism ring
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polynomial+ring"} polynomial ring
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}[\tfrac{1}{2}]
            on generators in degrees
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 4
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 4k
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo •
                    %mi SO
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 4
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 8
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 12
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Omega^{SO}_\bullet[\tfrac{1}{2}]
                  \\simeq
                  \\mathbb{Z}[\tfrac{1}{2}] [x_4, x_8, x_{12}, \cdots  ]
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_4
            is the class of the complex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+space"} projective space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℂ
                  %msup
                    %mi P
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}P^2
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 8
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_8
            that of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℍ
                  %msup
                    %mi P
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{H}P^2
            and where all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+genera"} elliptic genera
            vanish on all the other generators (
            %a{:href => "#LandweberRavenelStong93"}> Landweber-Ravenel-Stong 93, prop. 3.2
            ).
          %p
            From this one gets that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient"} quotient
            by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ideal"} ideal
            generated by these higher elements is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo •
                    %mi SO
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mrow
                      %mn 4
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi k
                      %mo ≥
                      %mn 3
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi MF
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo •
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi δ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ϵ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Omega^{SO}_\bullet[\tfrac{1}{2}]/(x_{4(k \geq 3)})
                  \\simeq
                  MF_0(2)_\bullet \coloneqq \mathbb{Z}[\tfrac{1}{2}][\delta, \epsilon]
          %p
            where the right hand side here is naturally identified as the ring of those
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modular+forms"} modular forms
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/congruence+subgroup"} congruence subgroup
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Γ
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma_0(2)
            which have half-integral
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
            in their
            = succeed "-expansion" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nodal+curve"} nodal curve
            (
            %a{:href => "#LandweberRavenelStong93"}> Landweber-Ravenel-Stong 93, theorem 1.5
            ).
          %p
            Now by a general construction due to (
            %a{:href => "#Baas73"}> Baas 73
            ) this induces a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+homology+theory"} generalized homology theory
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo •
                    %mi SO
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Omega^{SO}_\bullet[\tfrac{1}{2}](-)
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brown+representability+theorem"} represented
            by some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum"} spectrum
            = succeed ",whose" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ell
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ell
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Ell
                    %mo •
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi MF
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo •
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Ell_\bullet \simeq MF_0(2)_\bullet
                  \\,.
          %p By construction, this comes with a quotient map
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %mi SO
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi Ell
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  M SO[\tfrac{1}{2}] \longrightarrow Ell
          %p
            which is a map of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+spectra"} ring spectra
            by (
            %a{:href => "#Mironov78"}> Mironov 78
            ). This maplifts the universal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+genus"} elliptic genus
            (in that it reproduces it on
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups"} homotopy groups
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#LandweberRavenelStong93"} Landweber-Ravenel-Stong 93, section 4.6, 4.7
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#induced_relation_between_cobordism_and_homology Induced relation between cobordism and homology
          %p
            The SO orientation of elliptic cohomology makes it expressible in terms of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+cohomology+theory"} cobordism cohomology theory
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+theory+determining+homology+theory"} cobordism theory determining homology theory
            (
            %a{:href => "#LandweberRavenelStong93"}> Landweber-Ravenel-Stong 93, theorem 1.2
            ).
          %h3#relation_to_the_atiyahbottshapiro_spin_orientation_of_ko Relation to the Atiyah-Bott-Shapiro Spin orientation of KO
          %p There are maps of spectra
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ell
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi KO
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Ell [\epsilon^{-1}] \longrightarrow KO[\tfrac{1}{2}]
          %p and
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ell
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi δ
                    %mn 2
                  %mo −
                  %mi ϵ
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi KO
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
