          %h2#references References
          %p The construction is due to
          %ul
            %li#LandweberRavenelStong93
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Landweber"}> Peter Landweber
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Douglas+Ravenel"} Douglas Ravenel
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+Stong"} Robert Stong
              = succeed "," do
                %em Periodic cohomology theories defined by elliptic curves
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Haynes+Miller"} Haynes Miller
              et. al. (eds.),
              = succeed "," do
                %em The Cech centennial: A conference on homotopy theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.sciences.univ-nantes.fr/~hossein/GdT-Elliptique/Landweber-Ravenel-Stong.pdf"} pdf
          %p based on general constructions of multiplicative homology theories from cobordism theories due to
          %ul
            %li#Baas73
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nils+Baas"}> Nils Baas
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On bordism theory of manifolds with singularities
            %li#Mironov78
              %p
                O. K. Mironov,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Multiplications in cobordism theories with singularities
          %p
            Analysis of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ell
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ell
            is in
          %ul
            %li#Baker97
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrew+Baker"}> Andrew Baker
                , The homotopy type of the spectrum representing elliptic cohomology, Proceedings of the American Mathematical Society 107.2 (1989): 537-548. (
                %a{:href => "http://www.maths.gla.ac.uk/~ajb/dvi-ps/homell.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrew+Baker"}> Andrew Baker
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    On the Adams
                    = succeed "-term" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi E
                              %mn 2
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_2
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.maths.gla.ac.uk/~ajb/dvi-ps/ell-ext.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            The interpretation of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ell
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ell
            in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tmf0%282%29"} TMF0(2)
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#Behrens05
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mark+Behrens"}> Mark Behrens
              ,
              %em A modular description of the K(2)-local sphere at the prime 3
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0507184"}> arXiv:math/0507184
              )
          %p More is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dylan+Wilson"}> Dylan Wilson
              ,
              %em Orientations and Topological Modular Forms with Level Structure
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1507.05116"}> arXiv:1507.05116
              )
